Ima: You're home, anak. How did your training go?
You: It was harder than I expected. Chief says I still have more to learn.
Ima: That's only natural. No one becomes strong in a single day.
Ima: But you're home safely, and that's what matters to me.
Litik: Speaking of learning, there's another greeting you should remember.
Ima: Mayap a bengi, anak.
[signal arg="[signal arg="encounter_mayap_a_bengi"]"]
Litik: "Mayap a bengi" means "Good evening." You can use it when greeting someone in the evening.
You: Mayap a bengi, Ima.
[signal arg="[signal arg="learn_mayap_a_bengi"]"]
Ima: Mayap a bengi, anak. Now, get some rest.
Ima: Chief is waiting for you tomorrow. You need a clear head for your final training.
You: I will. Good night, Ima.
Ima: Sleep well, anak.
[signal arg="[signal arg="set_flag_sleep_transition_requested"]"]
[end_timeline]
